    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1111">

                <pb facs="1184" n="1088" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1088"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Straus.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic">September 20,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 5.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of Mr.
                    Riddle’s No. 179, of the 3d instant, transmitting translation of a note verbale
                    from the Sublime Porte on the subject of the regulations prohibiting the
                    entrance of Jews into Turkey.</p>
                <p>The dispatch has been anticipated by the Department sending the legation copies
                    of the correspondence on the subject with the Turkish minister here.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
